@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-validate-json-patch-operations-strictly-before-application
+type: decision-log
+title: "Validate JSON Patch operations strictly before application"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+JSON Patch input arrives at a public library boundary. Permissive operation or pointer handling could
+silently modify a location other than the caller intended.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate every operation's required members and JSON Pointer syntax before applying it. Apply each
+operation to a deep copy of the input document, using RFC 6901 token decoding and canonical array
+indexes. Reject attempts to remove the document root because the result would not be a JSON value.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Malformed patches and failed operations throw without mutating the supplied document. Object members
+may be added or replaced, while array insertion accepts only canonical indexes within the current
+array bounds or the RFC 6902 append token.
